            "block_content": "(1)(r) EMERGENCY ROOM COVERAGE – If a covered person utilizes emergency room services for non-emergency situations, as determined by the Claims Administrator, benefits will be reduced as outlined in the Traditional Plan document. Effective January 1, 2002, if services rendered in an emergency room are determined to be non-emergency by the Claims Administrator, benefits will be reduced by $75 with the remainder paid as outlined in the Traditional Plan document.",
